From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:47:32 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 44/45] inkling2: global prompt attention shares K/V tiles
 across 128 pairs

One stream's prompt rows on a global layer run a new kernel: a block of
128 (row, head) pairs shares each 64-key K/V tile through a three-stage
cp.async pipeline. Each pair keeps the split decode path's arithmetic, so
its partials and outputs are bit-identical to the fold kernel's.
